. * nwsaom tutorial 3: goodness of fit and fixing a poor model
. * Requires the core nwcommands and the package nwsaom.
. 
. nwwebuse glasgow, nwclear

. 
. * A deliberately thin model
. nwsaom, waves(glasgow1 glasgow2 glasgow3) outdegree reciprocity seed(1)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SAOM (Method of Moments, conditional), waves: glasgow1 glasgow2 glasgow3
Actors: 50                             Periods: 2
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
glasgow1_t~3 | Coefficient  Std. err.      z    P>|z|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
   outdegree |  -2.378798   .1097313   -21.68   0.000    -2.593868   -2.163729
 reciprocity |   2.860568     .18893    15.14   0.000     2.490272    3.230864
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rate parameters (estimated, one per inter-wave period):

             |   period1    period2 
-------------+---------------------
        rate |    5.7818     4.5006 
          se |    0.9153     0.6716 
Overall maximum convergence ratio: 0.054 (criterion: below 0.25; met)
Convergence t-ratios (criterion: all below 0.1 in absolute value): met

. estat gof, nsim(100) seed(7)

Goodness of fit: Mahalanobis distance test, 100 simulations at the estimates (2 periods pooled)

           statistic |   Mahalanobis  P-value      Fit
---------------------+--------------------------------
           Outdegree |         5.875    0.550       ok
            Indegree |         8.594    0.370       ok
            Geodesic |       209.758    0.000 rejected
------------------------------------------------------
Fit is rejected when P < 0.05 (one-tailed test).
Violin plots: gof_outdegree gof_indegree gof_geodesic

. graph export "gof_thin_geodesic.png", name(gof_geodesic) width(900) replace
file
    .../gof_thin_geodesic.png saved as PNG format

. 
. * Add transitive triplets and degree effects: better, but not enough
. nwsaom, waves(glasgow1 glasgow2 glasgow3) outdegree reciprocity transtrip indegpopularity outactivity seed(1)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SAOM (Method of Moments, conditional), waves: glasgow1 glasgow2 glasgow3
Actors: 50                             Periods: 2
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
glasgow1_to_g~3 | Coefficient  Std. err.      z    P>|z|     [95% conf. interval]
----------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
      outdegree |  -1.314935    .406812    -3.23   0.001    -2.112272   -.5175985
    reciprocity |   2.277673   .2019793    11.28   0.000     1.881801    2.673545
indegpopularity |  -.3762948   .2156656    -1.74   0.081    -.7989915     .046402
    outactivity |  -.1522856   .0496435    -3.07   0.002     -.249585   -.0549861
      transtrip |   .7932102   .0859546     9.23   0.000     .6247423    .9616781
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rate parameters (estimated, one per inter-wave period):

             |   period1    period2 
-------------+---------------------
        rate |    7.2036     5.5928 
          se |    1.3031     0.9747 
Overall maximum convergence ratio: 0.089 (criterion: below 0.25; met)
Convergence t-ratios (criterion: all below 0.1 in absolute value): met

. estat gof, nsim(100) seed(7)

Goodness of fit: Mahalanobis distance test, 100 simulations at the estimates (2 periods pooled)

           statistic |   Mahalanobis  P-value      Fit
---------------------+--------------------------------
           Outdegree |         3.318    0.870       ok
            Indegree |         6.876    0.490       ok
            Geodesic |        19.007    0.000 rejected
------------------------------------------------------
Fit is rejected when P < 0.05 (one-tailed test).
Violin plots: gof_outdegree gof_indegree gof_geodesic

. 
. * Add a smoother triadic closure effect (gwesp) and out-popularity
. nwsaom, waves(glasgow1 glasgow2 glasgow3) outdegree reciprocity gwesp(.69) transtrip indegpopularity outactivity outpo
> pularity seed(1)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SAOM (Method of Moments, conditional), waves: glasgow1 glasgow2 glasgow3
Actors: 50                             Periods: 2
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
glasgow1_to_g~3 | Coefficient  Std. err.      z    P>|z|     [95% conf. interval]
----------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
      outdegree |  -1.250331   .5142486    -2.43   0.015     -2.25824   -.2424224
    reciprocity |   2.865521   .3582165     8.00   0.000      2.16343    3.567613
indegpopularity |  -.3861618   .5134133    -0.75   0.452    -1.392433    .6201099
    outactivity |  -.1657485    .052155    -3.18   0.001    -.2679703   -.0635266
      transtrip |   -.452402   .4809604    -0.94   0.347    -1.395067    .4902631
      gwesp_.69 |   3.278733   1.322956     2.48   0.013     .6857865    5.871679
  outpopularity |  -.3304203   .3708519    -0.89   0.373    -1.057277    .3964361
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rate parameters (estimated, one per inter-wave period):

             |   period1    period2 
-------------+---------------------
        rate |    6.8290     5.2721 
          se |    1.2023     0.8919 
Overall maximum convergence ratio: 0.150 (criterion: below 0.25; met)
Convergence t-ratios (criterion: all below 0.1 in absolute value): met

. estat gof, nsim(100) seed(7)

Goodness of fit: Mahalanobis distance test, 100 simulations at the estimates (2 periods pooled)

           statistic |   Mahalanobis  P-value      Fit
---------------------+--------------------------------
           Outdegree |         3.688    0.830       ok
            Indegree |         4.087    0.790       ok
            Geodesic |         8.904    0.170       ok
------------------------------------------------------
Fit is rejected when P < 0.05 (one-tailed test).
Violin plots: gof_outdegree gof_indegree gof_geodesic

. graph export "gof_final_geodesic.png", name(gof_geodesic) width(900) replace
file
    .../gof_final_geodesic.png saved as PNG format

. 
. * The triad census, and one test per period
. estat gof, nsim(100) seed(7) stats(triad)

Goodness of fit: Mahalanobis distance test, 100 simulations at the estimates (2 periods pooled)

           statistic |   Mahalanobis  P-value      Fit
---------------------+--------------------------------
               Triad |        90.343    0.000 rejected
------------------------------------------------------
Fit is rejected when P < 0.05 (one-tailed test).
Violin plots: gof_triad

. estat gof, nsim(100) seed(7) stats(outdegree) join(off)

Goodness of fit: Mahalanobis distance test, 100 simulations at the estimates (one test per period)

           statistic |   Mahalanobis  P-value      Fit
---------------------+--------------------------------
Outdegree (period 1) |         3.863    0.730       ok
Outdegree (period 2) |         7.579    0.330       ok
------------------------------------------------------
Fit is rejected when P < 0.05 (one-tailed test).
Violin plots: gof_outdegree_p1 gof_outdegree_p2

